I wrote the test suite in `apps/api/test/image-digest-confirmed.test.ts`. It compiles with no errors under `npx tsc -p tsconfig.test.json`. Against the current seam, the 57 tests that call `resolveImageDigest` fail with `not implemented`, as expected. The other 6 already pass, because they test `parseEnv` and `GET /version`, which the spec says stay unchanged.

To check that the tests can be passed, I ran them against two throwaway implementations. One handles the timeout with `AbortSignal.timeout(1000)`, the other with `setTimeout` and an `AbortController`. All 63 tests passed on both. Those implementations only ever existed in the compiled `dist-test` output, which I rebuilt afterwards, so it is back to the throwing version. Git shows only the new test file added.

**How the tests work:**
- **No real network:** each test replaces the global `fetch` with a fake that serves `URI_A` and `URI_B` from a route table and records every request (URL and method). Any URL not in the table gets a "connection refused" error. The fake builds a real `Request`, so `"not a url"` is rejected with the same error real `fetch` gives.
- **No real clock:** the timeout tests use node:test's mocked `setTimeout`. Node's mock timers don't cover `AbortSignal.timeout`, so the tests also swap it for a version driven by the mocked clock. Either way of writing the timeout fires when the test moves the clock to 1000 ms. The tests check the call is still pending at 999 ms and has resolved to `undefined` by 2000 ms.
- **Coverage:** every spec scenario has a test for its main case plus one edge case. Every example row of the three scenario outlines (the "endpoint cannot be used" table and both digest-format tables) gets its own test. A few edge cases go slightly beyond the scenario text but follow from the spec's rules:
  - an `env` wrapper that records which keys are read, to check that only `ECS_CONTAINER_METADATA_URI_V4` is read;
  - an `ImageID` with more than one `@`;
  - status 300;
  - the older `ECS_CONTAINER_METADATA_URI` variable being ignored;
  - a check that nothing is written to the console when the endpoint can't be used.
- **`process.env`:** the two `[happy-6]` tests set and delete `process.env.ECS_CONTAINER_METADATA_URI_V4`, then restore its original value in a `finally` block.

63 tests in 1 file.
